WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.680
The first hurricane that I can really remember was Hurricane Flossy which was '56 or '57.

2
00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:12.480
It wasn't that bad a hurricane.

3
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:16.320
We were in our house and the water kept coming up, the wind kept coming up.

4
00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:26.060
So we moved from there and went stayed with an aunt who had a more substantial house that was right next to the Coast Guard station.

5
00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:30.500
It's now the town hall, but back in the 1950s it was the Coast Guard station.

6
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:40.100
As the water came up, the Coast Guard came over with one of their big old fashioned rowboats.

7
00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:53.240
The Coast Guard was out wading in the water pushing the boat and we had several people, a lot of them were really elderly people.

8
00:00:53.240 --> 00:01:05.480
We got them in the boat and the Coast Guard waded back and pulled us back to the station and we all rode the storm out in the Coast Guard station.

9
00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:11.620
That's the first . . . first real storm I remember.

10
00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:17.920
For Betsy, I was . . . Kind of ironic,

11
00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:22.620
I was serving in the Coast Guard at the time and I was stationed in New Jersey.

12
00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:26.320
I was being discharged and Betsy was in the Atlantic.

13
00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:30.500
The day I was discharged, I was in Cape May, New Jersey.

14
00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:35.560
I was married at the time and I remember telling my wife, "That's one storm we don't have to worry about,

15
00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:43.420
honey!" [laughing] So we came back and her parents lived on the West Bank in New Orleans.

16
00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:48.840
We got there and about a day later here comes Betsy tearing through there.

17
00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:51.840
And Betsy hit Grand Isle real bad.

18
00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:56.660
That's probably the worst storm we had there since the 1893 storm.

19
00:01:56.660 --> 00:02:03.440
So wasn't it some sort of tradition that if you stayed on the island, you got into the Coast Guard station?

20
00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:09.560
Yeah, that was the place to go because it was the most substantial building here.
